cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "feigen: stiffness eigenmodes of a single finite element"
type: software
abstract: >-
  feigen is a Fortran program and module that computes the stiffness matrix of
  a single isotropic linear elastic finite element and its eigenmodes. Zero
  eigenvalues reveal rigid-body and hourglass modes. Each mode is named by its
  best-matching displacement field (translation, rotation, expansion, shear,
  bending, torsion, warping, hourglass) and plotted, one subplot per mode, as
  PNG, SVG or PDF. It covers lines, triangles, quadrilaterals, tetrahedra,
  hexahedra and wedges of any order, is written in Fortran 2018 and builds with fpm.
authors:
